# The MQL5 sources are stored byte-exactly: no EOL conversion, no renormalising.
# nadir2.mq5 is CRLF because MetaEditor wrote it that way (39 792 lines), every
# QSMC header is LF. `text` would normalise the index to LF and turn the next
# `git pull` on a Windows box with core.autocrlf=true into a whole-file diff -
# the exact noise that hides a real change in a file this size.
*.mq5  -text
*.mqh  -text
*.py   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
